WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:17.104
"The parade starts in five minutes!"

2
00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:18.385
yelled Katie.

3
00:00:18.405 --> 00:00:20.565
"The wagons are ready!"

4
00:00:20.966 --> 00:00:21.706
called Joy.

5
00:00:22.206 --> 00:00:24.587
The twins ran to the front of the parade.

6
00:00:25.727 --> 00:00:26.567
Mr. and Mrs.

7
00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:29.248
Pinker sat up high in a covered wagon.

8
00:00:30.428 --> 00:00:32.610
The Pinker children crowded behind them.

9
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:37.633
"They're traveling just like Howard Lightfoot Jackson and his family!"

10
00:00:38.073 --> 00:00:38.814
cried Joy.

11
00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.676
"Who?" asked Katie.

12
00:00:41.696 --> 00:00:44.558
"The first family in Willow Creek!"

13
00:00:45.038 --> 00:00:45.798
answered Joy.

14
00:00:45.818 --> 00:00:49.321
"Huh?" Katie stared at her twin.

15
00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:50.762
"What do you mean?"

16
00:00:52.403 --> 00:00:54.544
Before Joy could answer, Mr.

17
00:00:54.584 --> 00:00:57.746
Pinker shook the reins and his horses started moving.

18
00:00:58.967 --> 00:00:59.988
AJ came running.

19
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.261
"Katie! Ms.

20
00:01:02.301 --> 00:01:03.562
Henderson is here!"

21
00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:04.603
he yelled.

22
00:01:04.623 --> 00:01:06.604
"She's in the Model T!"

23
00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:09.666
"Who?" asked Joy.

24
00:01:09.686 --> 00:01:12.888
"The oldest person in Willow Creek!"

25
00:01:13.449 --> 00:01:14.229
said AJ.

26
00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:17.211
"What?" cried Joy.

27
00:01:21.354 --> 00:01:22.695
kids!" Ms.

28
00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.636
Henderson called.

29
00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:26.017
"I've come to the parade!"

30
00:01:26.037 --> 00:01:32.754
"Let's get this car started," said Grandpa Henderson, rubbing his hands together.

31
00:01:32.774 --> 00:01:36.918
"First, we pull this and turn that."

32
00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:42.262
Grandpa Henderson jumped out of the car and hurried around to the front.

33
00:01:42.282 --> 00:01:46.686
"Now I turn and pull this handle."

34
00:01:47.266 --> 00:01:48.707
He turned and pulled.

35
00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:52.591
"It started!"

36
00:01:53.111 --> 00:01:54.112
everyone shouted.

37
00:01:54.132 --> 00:01:58.716
"It just takes practice," said Grandpa Henderson.

38
00:02:00.396 --> 00:02:01.896
"It's running away!"

39
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:03.597
everyone screamed.

40
00:02:04.137 --> 00:02:06.738
The Model T began rolling toward the street.

41
00:02:06.758 --> 00:02:08.778
"Get in!"

42
00:02:09.358 --> 00:02:10.019
cried Ms.

43
00:02:10.059 --> 00:02:15.300
Henderson. Grandpa Henderson jumped in the car beside his sister.

44
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.521
"Here we go!"

45
00:02:18.061 --> 00:02:18.761
he shouted.

46
00:02:18.781 --> 00:02:21.902
"See you at the park!"

47
00:02:22.582 --> 00:02:23.822
called the Earthworms.

48
00:02:25.123 --> 00:02:29.544
The high school marching band lined up behind a giant birthday cake.

49
00:02:30.768 --> 00:02:31.829
Then Mrs.

50
00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:33.509
Penkov blew her whistle.

51
00:02:33.529 --> 00:02:36.270
"Campers!" she called.

52
00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.571
"Get into place behind the band!"

53
00:02:39.812 --> 00:02:42.193
Emily and Carlos unrolled the banner.

54
00:02:42.213 --> 00:02:45.594
"The Willow Creek Day Campers!"

55
00:02:46.155 --> 00:02:46.895
read Katie.

56
00:02:46.915 --> 00:02:48.216
"That's us!"

57
00:02:49.576 --> 00:02:51.217
The band started playing.

58
00:02:54.018 --> 00:02:55.919
Luke climbed onto his stilts.

59
00:02:55.939 --> 00:02:58.600
"Woo-hoo!" he yelled.

60
00:02:59.772 --> 00:03:02.234
The day campers headed toward Main Street.

61
00:03:03.935 --> 00:03:06.836
As they turned the corner, Joy saw her family.

62
00:03:06.856 --> 00:03:09.258
"Mom, Dad!"

63
00:03:09.758 --> 00:03:12.339
she shouted, waving her ribbon twirler.

64
00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:17.302
"Grandpa!" Aunt Sally stood outside Fried Pie Heaven.

65
00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:20.044
"Hello, Aunt Sally!"

66
00:03:20.604 --> 00:03:22.025
shouted Katie and Joy.

67
00:03:23.386 --> 00:03:27.408
They turned onto Walnut Street and paraded into the town park.

68
00:03:28.564 --> 00:03:33.168
The band kept playing while everyone ate watermelon and drank lemonade.

69
00:03:34.249 --> 00:03:39.254
Then the mayor made a speech, and the Willow Creek Singers performed old songs.

70
00:03:40.535 --> 00:03:41.816
Finally Mrs.

71
00:03:41.896 --> 00:03:45.319
Penkov stepped onto the platform to address the crowd.

72
00:03:45.339 --> 00:03:51.344
"As you know, the day campers had a scavenger hunt this summer."

73
00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.246
"Yes, they did.

74
00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:54.988
And they were real pests!"

75
00:03:55.604 --> 00:03:57.965
Pete from the post office shouted, laughing.

76
00:03:58.525 --> 00:03:59.745
The crowd laughed too.

77
00:04:01.906 --> 00:04:03.406
Mrs. Penkov continued.

78
00:04:03.426 --> 00:04:06.067
"Now it's time to announce the winners.

79
00:04:06.547 --> 00:04:07.127
Guess what?"

80
00:04:10.008 --> 00:04:11.569
The campers held their breath.

81
00:04:11.589 --> 00:04:15.150
"We have a tie!"

82
00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.490
The campers gasped.

83
00:04:18.831 --> 00:04:20.651
"Two teams completed their lists.

84
00:04:21.111 --> 00:04:23.052
Both found Willow Creek treasures.

85
00:04:24.428 --> 00:04:30.832
One team found a piece of history—the oldest grave in Willow Creek at the burial place of the

86
00:04:30.913 --> 00:04:32.414
first settling family."

87
00:04:33.494 --> 00:04:35.936
Mrs. Penkov unrolled a crayon rubbing.

88
00:04:35.956 --> 00:04:39.078
"Howard Lightfoot Jackson,1848."

89
00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:46.383
"The other team found a living treasure— our oldest citizen," continued Mrs.

90
00:04:46.443 --> 00:04:50.506
Penkov. "Cora Mae Henderson—103 years old.

91
00:04:50.546 --> 00:04:56.458
So the winners are the Tornadoes and the Earthworms!

92
00:04:57.679 --> 00:05:02.123
Each team member wins a ticket for a free day at Big Surf Water Park!"

93
00:05:02.543 --> 00:05:03.144
said Mrs.

94
00:05:03.224 --> 00:05:06.406
Penkov. "Big Surf!"

95
00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.189
cried the Tornadoes and the Earthworms.

96
00:05:09.209 --> 00:05:11.571
"The Double Dip!"

97
00:05:12.131 --> 00:05:13.552
cried Joy and Laura.

98
00:05:13.572 --> 00:05:16.315
"The Slippery Spin!"

99
00:05:16.815 --> 00:05:18.156
cried Katie and Luke.

100
00:05:19.377 --> 00:05:22.420
The Tornadoes and the Earthworms jumped with joy.

101
00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.862
Later that evening, they sat beside the creek and watched fireworks explode in the sky.

102
00:05:30.882 --> 00:05:35.364
"Day camp is over," said Joy with a sigh.

103
00:05:35.384 --> 00:05:40.867
"But we have Willow Creek T-shirts to keep forever," said Laura.

104
00:05:40.887 --> 00:05:44.628
"And we all won the scavenger hunt!"

105
00:05:45.048 --> 00:05:45.689
said Luke.

106
00:05:45.709 --> 00:05:49.350
"And we all get to go to Big Surf!"

107
00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:50.651
said AJ.

108
00:05:51.671 --> 00:05:52.551
Katie grinned.

109
00:05:52.571 --> 00:05:58.663
"Best of all, we still have the rest of the summer to have fun in our Willow Creek!"
